Base model
----------

This model is a modified version of the tessdata_best Hebrew model
(heb.traineddata) of the Tesseract OCR project,
https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_best, commit
e12c65a915945e4c28e237a9b52bc4a8f39a0cec, sha256
dbaa827aea6bc21215638447f17783a1004987c2d0bf5573d111fee397abdae5, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

HeOCR modified it in two stages. HeOCR R7 (2026-11-11) fine-tuned its LSTM
network on real scanned Hebrew lines. R8b (2026-11-12) continued training
from R7's weights on more real lines, rendered born-digital lines and
synthetic lines. Five characters were added to the base's character set: the
maqaf U+05BE, the en dash U+2013, the geresh U+05F3, the gershayim U+05F4
and the em dash U+2014. The dictionary components were rebuilt from the
base model's own word list with build files from
https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/langdata_lstm, commit
07930fd9f246622c26eb5de794d9212ceac432d3, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. No word list was built from any training text.

Software
--------

The model was trained with, and runs in, Tesseract 5.5.3
(https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. The model file contains no Tesseract code.

