Training data: Hebrew Wikisource (text) and Wikimedia Commons (scan)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Eleven training lines come from one Hebrew Wikisource proofread page
(line set wslines_v1): Salomon Buber (d. 1906), Sifrei de-Agadeta al
Megillat Ester, Vilna, 1886, page 136. The scan is
File:Salomon Buber. Sifre de-agadeta al megilat Ester.1886.pdf on Wikimedia
Commons (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salomon_Buber._Sifre_de-agadeta_al_megilat_Ester.1886.pdf;
an Internet Archive scan from a copy at Robarts - University of Toronto,
not digitized by Google), the route HeOCR's legal strategy calls
wikimedia_commons; its rights justification is
rj:ws_index_332490:0b20c1d7e01b. The labels are the proofread
transcription by Hebrew Wikisource contributors,
https://he.wikisource.org/w/index.php?oldid=763704, licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 licence (CC BY-SA 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Per heocr-engine decision
0016 the weights stay Apache-2.0 with this credit, and no word list or dawg
was built from Wikisource text: the model's word list is the base model's.

Training data: synthetic lines
------------------------------

18,627 synthetic lines are HeOCR's s17a_addon_v1.1 set (CC0 1.0): images
made by HeOCR's S17a generator, trained from scratch by HeOCR, from renders
in the Frank Ruhl Libre typeface (SIL Open Font License 1.1; the font is
not distributed with the model), styled after line crops from 29 of the
NLI and Internet Archive books above (all university-library or NLI scans;
none digitized by Google). Their text is from Project Ben-Yehuda. The
generator and the set's build recipe are in HeOCR/hocrsyngen
(https://github.com/HeOCR/hocrsyngen), commit
3b55d4aff3de9f3211bc1573f2e0644748e84d63, under
experiments/learned_generation_v0/s17a_scanifier/.

Training data: text
-------------------

The scanned book lines and the synthetic lines are labelled with
transcriptions from Project Ben-Yehuda (https://benyehuda.org), public
domain dump release 2026-03
(https://github.com/projectbenyehuda/public_domain_dump). Its licence states
that the data files are in the public domain. Credit: Project Ben-Yehuda
volunteers.

The model contains no scan images, no rendered pages and no text files. The
line crops are not distributed with it.

Evaluation data (not used for training)
---------------------------------------

The model was scored on held-out lines whose reference text comes from
these sources. They were used only to choose and score the model, never for
training:
  - lines of scanned Reshumot booklets labelled with the text of ספר החוקים
    הפתוח on Hebrew Wikisource (CC BY-SA 4.0, Hebrew Wikisource
    contributors), and Hebrew Wikisource proofread pages (CC BY-SA 4.0);
  - Project Ben-Yehuda transcriptions of further Internet Archive and NLI
    scans (public domain);
  - rendered Reshumot booklets (PD-IL);
  - a Sefaria transcription of an Internet Archive scan (public domain).
The model contains no evaluation text.

